name:    fzf
what:    using the picker in a pipe, which is where it earns its place
check:   fzf
install: sudo dnf install fzf   /   sudo apt install fzf
docs:    fzf --help, man fzf
probe:   help

= USING IT IN A PIPE
ls \| fzf        | pick a file, print the name
cd $(find . -type d \| fzf) | pick a directory and go there
git branch \| fzf | pick a branch
rg -l text \| fzf | pick from the files that matched
fzf --preview 'bat --color=always {}' | show the file as you move through
fzf -m           | allow picking several with Tab
fzf -q text      | start with the query already typed
fzf -1           | if exactly one thing matches, take it without asking

= ALL FLAGS (from --help)
